  era: "3rd c. BCE \xB7 Section 7 \xB7 Mauryan Empire \xB7 c. 321 \u2013 185 BCE"
  title: Mauryan economy
  text: The state controlled mines, forests and many industries, collected land revenue of about a quarter of the produce, and regulated trade, weights and prices. Punch-marked silver coins circulated widely, and roads linked the empire.
